# Bluetooth is not a product feature. Remove the stack from the kernel so the
# radio driver simply does not exist in the shipped image — hci_uart then
# cannot bind no matter what the device tree says.
#
# This is the product's ONLY Bluetooth off-switch, and it is the stronger claim
# for the RED radio assessment: absence of a driver rather than a disabled
# device-tree node. Do not weaken it without replacing the mechanism —
# scripts/assert-release-image.sh asserts the bluetooth module tree is absent
# from the built rootfs.
#
# The image also ships no BT firmware (BR2_PACKAGE_BRCMFMAC_SDIO_FIRMWARE_RPI_WIFI
# installs the Wi-Fi blobs only) and no bluez userspace, so this is the third
# of three independent legs. Applied to both boards from this one file.
# CONFIG_BT is not set
# CONFIG_BT_HCIUART is not set
# CONFIG_BT_HCIBTUSB is not set
# CONFIG_TI_ST is not set
